   "id": "bb-303-scheme",
   "h": "Diplopia scheme (Blackbook)",
   "html": "<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b303a\"></div><div class=\"pearl\"><p><b>Clinical Pearls:</b></p><ul><li>Diplopia is almost always binocular.</li><li>CN VI palsy is a red flag for intracranial masses.</li><li>Look for ptosis with CN III palsy.</li><li>Examine both eyes to determine which is affected.</li><li>Neurologic symptoms suggest a mass as the cause.</li><li>Myasthenia Gravis is fatiguable.</li><li>Migraine is a diagnosis of exclusion.</li></ul></div>"
  }
 ],
